  <!-- Where conventional testing stops -->
  <section id="limits" class="section" aria-labelledby="limits-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="limits-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">Where conventional testing stops</h2>
      <ul class="audiences mt-10">
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Screening tests</h3>
          <p>Quick and cheap, but every positive result needs a second, confirmatory test. In a district programme the second test is often the one that never happens.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">Confirmatory tests</h3>
          <p>One to two millilitres of venous blood, a cold chain to the laboratory, pre-processing before the assay, and a laboratory that few districts have. For a newborn, a wait of 72 hours.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3 class="h3">What a programme needs</h3>
          <p>A sample a health worker can take anywhere, a result that needs no second test, a laboratory within reach, and a cost that works for a whole population.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Compared: the poster's table, without its sensitivity and specificity rows (content 2.1) -->
  <section id="compared" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="compared-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="compared-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">The same question, three ways of answering it</h2>
        <p class="lead lg:col-span-5">How <span class="whitespace-nowrap">LitLife™</span> compares with the tests a programme would otherwise use.</p>
      </div>
      <table class="compare-table mt-12" aria-labelledby="compared-h">
        <caption>From our presentation to the haematology community, October 2026.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <td></td>
            <th scope="col">Conventional screening tests</th>
            <th scope="col">Conventional confirmatory tests</th>
            <th scope="col" class="is-ours">LitLife™</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {%- set compared = [
            ["Sample", "20 to 50 µl of blood", "1 to 2 ml of EDTA blood", "A spot of blood on a card"],
            ["Collection", "Finger prick", "Venepuncture", "Finger prick"],
            ["Storage and transport", "Cold chain", "Cold chain", "Room temperature"],
            ["Pre-processing", "Yes", "Yes", "None"],
            ["Throughput", "Low", "Low", "High"],
            ["A second test to confirm", "Yes", "No", "No"],
            ["Newborns", "No", "After 72 hours of birth", "At birth"]
          ] %}
          {%- for row in compared %}
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{{ row[0] }}</th>
            <td data-label="Conventional screening tests">{{ row[1] }}</td>
            <td data-label="Conventional confirmatory tests">{{ row[2] }}</td>
            <td data-label="LitLife™" class="is-ours">{{ row[3] }}</td>
          </tr>
          {%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The method: the poster's six steps. Steps 1 and 2 are the film's stills until the company's
       photographs arrive; 3 to 6 are representative photographs of the same work (CREDITS.md), labelled so under the steps. -->
  <section id="method" class="section" aria-labelledby="method-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="method-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">From card to result in six steps</h2>
      <!-- [html-validate-disable-next no-redundant-role, prefer-native-element: preflight's list-style: none drops the list role in Safari/VoiceOver] -->
      <ol role="list" class="steps-numbered mt-12">
        <li>
          <img src="/assets/img/site-drop.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="A drawn dried blood spot card held open, with a drop of blood falling towards its dashed collection circle." loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <h3 class="h3">Collect</h3>
          <p>A health worker cleans the fingertip, pricks it with a single-use lancet and lets the blood fall into the circle on the card.</p>
          <p>The spot dries, the cover closes over it, and the card travels at room temperature.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <img src="/assets/img/site-batch.webp" width="1000" height="1000" alt="The drawn card, closed, set down in a grid of many others, each with the Lightening Lives logo and a barcode." loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          <h3 class="h3">Punch</h3>
          <p>In the laboratory a small punch takes a disc from the dried spot straight into a PCR tube. There is no DNA extraction step.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{ picture("lab-pipette", "A multichannel pipette dispensing into a 96-well plate on a laboratory bench.", stepSizes) }}
          <h3 class="h3">Prepare</h3>
          <p>The reaction mix is specific to the mutation being looked for.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{ picture("lab-thermal-cycler", "A benchtop PCR thermal cycler with its lid open and a full rack of tubes in its block.", stepSizes) }}
          <h3 class="h3">Amplify</h3>
          <p>PCR, on a standard thermal cycler. Many cards run in one batch.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{ picture("lab-gel", "Gloved hands at a horizontal agarose gel electrophoresis tank, its leads running to a power supply.", stepSizes) }}
          <h3 class="h3">Separate</h3>
          <p>Agarose gel electrophoresis.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          {{ picture("lab-bench", "A gloved hand steadying a rack of open tubes while a pipette dispenses into one.", stepSizes) }}
          <h3 class="h3">Read</h3>
          <p>The result is visualised and interpreted, with controls alongside: affected, carrier or unaffected.</p>
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="steps-note">Photographs of steps 3 to 6 are representative images, not pictures of our own laboratory.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- What a laboratory needs -->
  <section id="laboratory" class="section bg-paper" aria-labelledby="laboratory-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="laboratory-h" class="h2 max-w-[44rem]">What a laboratory needs</h2>
      <ul class="rows mt-10">
        <li>
          <h3>Equipment</h3>
          <p>A thermal cycler, a gel electrophoresis tank and a punch: the equipment of a district or hospital laboratory, not a genetics institute.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>Space and storage</h3>
          <p>A bench. Cards keep at room temperature, so no cold chain for samples.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h3>People</h3>
          <p>Laboratory staff who have run PCR before, or who have been trained. We train them.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Monitoring -->
  <section id="monitoring" class="section" aria-labelledby="monitoring-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:items-start">
        <h2 id="monitoring-h" class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Seeing the programme as it happens</h2>
        <p class="text-moss lg:col-span-5">Test details are captured on a mobile app at the point of collection, so a programme can follow its screening in real time: how many samples, from where, and what came back.</p>
